FIX FE RACE-MODE DIALOG (816): reconstruct nested-table handlers 0x452bb4/bd4/c0c/c24 + int-typed setups

Pressing the race-options button (main screen 0, action FUN_004529b0 @0x4529b0) opens a
nested race-MODE dialog dispatched through a second screen table @0x46a374 (3 records:
Wrecking Racing / Stock Car / Destruction Derby). Two defects made it trap on wasm:

(1) Ghidra exported only record 0's handlers (FUN_00452b94 setup + FUN_00452bf4 action);
records 1/2 stayed raw code VAs (0x452bb4/0x452bd4 setups, 0x452c0c/0x452c24 actions), so
FUN_004529b0's dispatch jumped to unrelocated addresses. Reconstructed 1:1 from asm
0x452bb4-0x452c3d (setups point label slots 0x46a340/0x46a354 at the Stock Car / Destruction
Derby strings 0x46ee18/0x46ee2c + Setup_Screen_Text; actions FUN_00452f80 / Select_RaceType_DD
confirm-gate then race_mode = 1/2 @0x4673f8). Registered in dd2_dispatch.c; new string macros
in dd2_symbols.h.

(2) The nested dispatch types SETUP handlers as `code`=int() (`(*(code*)PTR_FUN_0046a374)()`
and `(*(code*)(&PTR_FUN_0046a374)[uVar3*5])()`), unlike the MAIN table @0x4697cc which casts
void(*)(void). FUN_00452b94 was void(void) -> return-type mismatch -> call_indirect trap the
instant the dialog opened (even record 0). Widened all three setups to int(void) (return 0,
discarded). The actions are bool = i32 return, which already matches int(). Signature-
normalization class (patches 610/765/785/815).

